● Real Life Scenarios — Workflows vs Agents

  ---
  Scenario 1: Customer Support System

  As a Workflow

  A telecom company handles 10,000 support tickets daily.

  Customer submits ticket
          │
          ▼
  Step 1: Classify ticket
          (billing / technical / cancellation)
          │
          ▼
  Step 2: Route to specialist prompt
          │
          ▼
  Step 3: Generate response using template
          │
          ▼
  Step 4: Check response tone and policy compliance
          │
          ▼
  Step 5: Send response to customer

  Why workflow here?
  - Same process every time
  - Needs to be consistent and auditable
  - High volume — must be fast and cheap
  - Failure must be predictable

  As an Agent

  A VIP enterprise client calls with a complex issue.

  Agent receives: "Our entire team lost access yesterday,
  we have a board presentation in 2 hours"

  Agent decides:
    → Check account status (tool call)
    → Finds account flagged for non-payment
    → Checks payment history (tool call)
    → Finds it was a billing system error
    → Escalates flag removal (tool call)
    → Restores access (tool call)
    → Drafts apology email
    → Notifies account manager
    → Logs incident report

  Why agent here?
  - Problem was unknown upfront
  - Required investigation and judgment
  - Steps depended on what was discovered
  - High stakes — needed flexible response

  ---
  Scenario 2: Content Marketing Pipeline

  As a Workflow

  A media company publishes 50 articles per day.

  Raw topic idea
        │
        ▼
  Step 1: Research — pull top 5 articles on topic
        │
        ▼
  Step 2: Outline — generate structured outline
        │
        ▼
  Step 3: Write — expand outline into full article
        │
        ▼
  Step 4: Edit — improve clarity and tone
        │
        ▼
  Step 5: SEO check — optimize keywords and metadata
        │
        ▼
  Step 6: Format — apply blog template
        │
        ▼
  Published article

  Why workflow here?
  - Same steps every single article
  - Easy to QA each step independently
  - Scales to 50 articles without human involvement
  - Consistent quality and brand voice

  As an Agent

  A journalist investigates a breaking news story.

  Agent receives: "Investigate the sudden resignation
  of the CFO at TechCorp"

  Agent decides:
    → Search recent news (tool call)
