      ▼
  Step 3: Generate packing slip
        │
        ▼
  Step 4: Assign to warehouse
        │
        ▼
  Step 5: Send tracking email

  Why workflow here?
  - Every order follows the same logic
  - Must be reliable — money involved
  - Speed critical at scale
  - Auditability required for disputes

  As an Agent

  Handling a complex return and fraud investigation.

  Agent receives: "Customer claims 10 orders arrived
  damaged over the past 3 months"

  Agent decides:
    → Pull all 10 order records (tool call)
    → Check delivery photos (tool call)
    → Finds 3 have proof of damage, 7 don't
    → Cross-references customer return history (tool call)
    → Checks if same delivery driver on all orders (tool call)
    → Finds pattern — same driver, same route
    → Flags driver for logistics review
